# How to install Postgres on your local  
  1. 'install brew and update it frist'
      brew update
  2.  Install Postgres using below command
      brew install postgresql@15

      Note : We can change the Postgres Version from as per the requirement @15, @16, @17, @18...

  3. Verify the installation. 
      /opt/homebrew/opt/postgresql@15/bin/postgres --version

      expected output will be : postgres (PostgreSQL) 15.x
  3. Add PostgreSQL 15 to your PATH
      For your MacBook, check the Homebrew location:
      brew --prefix
      
      If it returns /opt/homebrew, run:
      echo 'export PATH="/opt/homebrew/opt/postgresql@15/bin:$PATH"' >> ~/.zshrc
      source ~/.zshrc
      
      
      Verify:
      psql --version

  4.  Start Postgres 15 
      brew services start postgresql@15

  5.  to check the active service  
      brew services list

  6.  To login in the database 
      psql -h localhost -d salesdb -p 5432 -U rishabh
